# Normalize line endings for every text file to LF inside the repository, and check them out as
# LF regardless of OS/editor/core.autocrlf settings. Without this, files edited on Windows (CRLF)
# vs. this repo's existing LF content show as a full-file rewrite in `git diff`/`git status` purely
# from line-ending differences, not real changes -- exactly what's been happening repeatedly with
# .github/workflows/pages.yml. This makes that class of noise-diff impossible going forward, for
# every file, for every contributor, on every OS.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary/asset types some contributor might one day add -- explicitly marked so Git never attempts
# line-ending normalization on them (which would corrupt the file).
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.pptx binary
*.ods binary
*.zip binary
